---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_AUTHOR } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <article class="prose container-prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I'm {SITE_AUTHOR}. I write for a global, multilingual audience: crisp
      sentences, plain English, no walls of text.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site is an experiment in <strong>reading first</strong>. Most of the
      web fights for your attention. These notes try the opposite — calm
      typography, no popups, no cookie banners, no autoplaying anything, and no
      third-party trackers. Pages ship zero JavaScript unless an idea genuinely
      needs to move.
    </p>
    <h2>When prose isn't enough</h2>
    <p>
      Some ideas are processes, not paragraphs. For those, the page hydrates a
      small interactive “island”: a stepper to walk a concept, a replayable
      sequence diagram you can scrub, or a loop you can watch cycle. Each one is
      keyboard-operable, respects reduced-motion, and degrades to a static
      frame with a full text description when scripting is off.
    </p>
    <h2>Principles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Body text at a comfortable size, generous line-height, a ~65-character measure.</li>
      <li>Light and dark are both first-class; the light theme is warm, never glaring.</li>
      <li>Contrast targets WCAG AAA for body text where feasible.</li>
      <li>Every element earns its place — decorative chrome doesn't ship.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .container-prose {
    max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--content-pad));
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--content-pad);
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }
  .container-prose h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }
</style>
